==English==
{{was wotd|2023|August|28}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|ḱóm}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰregʰ-|*-tis}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|contraccioun}}, {{m|enm|contraxion|t=spasm, contraction; constriction, shrinking; act of pressing together}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=contracciǒun|pos=n|id=MED9549}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|contraction}} (modern {{cog|fr|contraction}}), from {{der|en|la|contractiō|t=a drawing together, contraction; abridgement, shortening; dejection, despondency|alt=contractiō(n)}}, from {{m|la|contrahō|t=to draw things together, assemble, collect, gather; to enter into a contract}}<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=40343|date=March 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220529023518/https://www.lexico.com/definition/contraction}}</ref> + {{m|la|-tiō|-tiō(n)|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|noun}}s relating to actions or their results}}. {{m|la|contrahō|Contrahō}} is derived from {{m|la|con-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} denoting a bringing together of objects}} + {{m|la|trahō|t=to drag, pull}} (probably from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰregʰ-|t=to drag, pull; to run}}). {{surf|+suf|en|contract|ion|pos2=suffix denoting actions or processes, or their results}}.

