===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{non-gloss|Senses relating to [[become|becoming]] [[involve]]d with or [[enter#Verb|entering]] into, especially entering into a [[contract#Noun|contract]].}}
## {{senseid|en|acquisition generally}} An [[act#Noun|act]] of [[incur]]ring [[debt]]; also {{lb|en|generally}}, an act of [[acquire|acquiring]] something (generally [[negative#Adjective|negative]]).
##: {{ux|en|Our '''contraction''' of debt in this quarter has reduced our ability to attract investors.}}
## {{lb|en|archaic}} An act of entering into a contract or [[agreement]]; specifically, a contract of [[marriage]]; a [[contracting#Noun|contracting]]; also {{lb|en|obsolete}}, a [[betrothal]].
## {{senseid|en|acquiring of a disease}}{{lb|en|biology|medicine}} The [[process#Noun|process]] of [[contract#Verb|contracting]] or becoming [[infect#Verb|infected]] with a [[disease#Noun|disease]].
##: {{synonyms|en|acquiring|catching}}
##: {{ux|en|the '''contraction''' of malaria}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|author=David Turner|title=How Railway Staff were Conduits and Victims of a Pandemic|magazine=[[w:Rail (magazine)|Rail]]|location=Peterborough, Cambridgeshire|publisher=[[w:Bauer Media Group|Bauer Media]]|date=8 April 2020|page=32|issn=0953-4563|oclc=999467860|passage=Railway workers were therefore a perfect subject for research, given the varied roles they undertook. If infection was greatest among the non-public-facing staff, it would suggest&nbsp;– given most worked outside&nbsp;– that '''contraction''' was caused by something found in the "atmosphere at large". If affliction was higher among the indoor and public-facing staff, it would suggest that human contact was the cause. And it was the latter point that was proven.}}
# {{non-gloss|Senses relating to [[pull#Verb|pulling]] together or [[shorten]]ing.}}
## {{senseid|en|reduction in size}} A (sometimes [[reversible#Adjective|reversible]]) contracting or [[reduction]] in [[length#Noun|length]], [[scope#Noun|scope]], [[size#Noun|size]], or [[volume#Noun|volume]]; a [[narrowing#Noun|narrowing]], a [[shortening#Noun|shortening]], a [[shrinking#Noun|shrinking]].
##: {{antonyms|en|dilatation|dilation|expansion}}
### {{lb|en|archaic|or|obsolete}} An [[abridgement]] or shortening of [[writing#Noun|writing]], etc.; an [[abstract#Noun|abstract]], a [[summary#Noun|summary]]; also {{lb|en|uncountable}}, [[brevity]], [[conciseness]].
###: {{sense|abridgement or shortening of writing, etc.}} {{synonyms|en|condensation|epitome}}
### {{senseid|en|phase of wound healing}}{{lb|en|biology|medicine}} A [[stage#Noun|stage]] of [[wound#Noun|wound]] [[healing#Noun|healing]] during which the wound [[edge#Noun|edges]] are [[gradually]] [[pull#Verb|pulled]] together.
### {{senseid|en|shortening of any muscle}}{{lb|en|biology|medicine}} A shortening of a [[muscle#Noun|muscle]] during its [[use#Noun|use]]; specifically, a [[strong#Adjective|strong]] and often [[painful]] shortening of the [[uterine#Adjective|uterine]] muscles prior to or during [[childbirth]].
###* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Laurence Street|title=Introduction to Biomedical Engineering Technology|page=125|passage=Though occasionally a “flatliner” can be revived with a defib, it is most commonly used to change the uncoordinated '''contractions''' of the heart (fibrillation) into a normal sinus rhythm—that is, to defibrillate the heart.}}
### {{senseid|en|economics}}{{lb|en|economics}} A [[period#Noun|period]] of [[economic]] [[decline#Noun|decline]] or negative [[growth]].
###: {{ux|en|The country’s economic '''contraction''' was caused by high oil prices.}}
### {{senseid|en|linguistics}}{{lb|en|linguistics}} A process whereby one or more [[sound#Noun|sounds]] of a [[free morpheme]] (a [[word#Noun|word]]) are [[reduce]]d or [[lose#Verb|lost]], such that it becomes a [[bound morpheme]] (a [[clitic]]) that [[attach]]es [[phonologically]] to an [[adjacent#Adjective|adjacent]] word.
###: {{hyponyms|en|apheresis|apocope|elision|syncope}}
###: {{ux|en|In the English words ''didn’t'', ''that’s'', and ''wanna'', the endings ''-n’t'', ''-’s'', and ''-a'' arose by '''contraction'''.}}
### {{senseid|en|phonetics}}{{lb|en|linguistics|phonology|prosody}} {{synonym of|en|syncope|t=the [[elision]] or [[loss#Noun|loss]] of a [[sound#Noun|sound]] from the [[interior#Noun|interior]] of a [[word#Noun|word]], especially of a [[vowel#Noun|vowel]] sound with loss of a [[syllable#Noun|syllable]]}}
### {{c|en|Algebra}}{{lb|en|ring theory|of an [[ideal]] in the [[codomain]] of a [[ring]] [[homomorphism]]}} The [[preimage]] of the given ideal under the given homomorphism.
### {{senseid|en|orthography}}{{lb|en|orthography}} In the [[English#Adjective|English]] [[language]]: a shortened [[form#Noun|form]] of a word, often with [[omitted#Adjective|omitted]] [[letter#Noun|letters]] [[replace]]d by an [[apostrophe]] or a [[diacritical mark]].
###: {{ux|en|''Don’t'' is a '''contraction''' of ''do not''; and ''’til'' is a '''contraction''' of ''until''.}}
### {{senseid|en|shorthand symbol}}{{lb|en|by extension}} A [[shorthand#Noun|shorthand]] [[symbol#Noun|symbol]] [[indicate|indicating]] an [[omission]] for the [[purpose#Noun|purpose]] of brevity.
## {{lb|en|obsolete|rare}} An act of [[collect#Verb|collecting]] or [[gather#Verb|gathering]].

